    "policy_notes": [
      "Validated workflow specification DRAGON under project policy cf89ad9eddd6.",
      "Use CSV or TSV with a header; the first column is a unique sample ID and every remaining column is a unique feature ID.",
      "Rows are samples and columns are features in both layers. Layer 2 is reordered to layer 1 only after exact sample-ID set equality is proven.",
      "Values must be finite continuous numeric measurements. Missing values, non-numeric fields, duplicate sample IDs, and duplicate feature IDs are rejected; no imputation or normalization is implicit.",
      "The verified API has no sample_metadata, motif, PPI, expression-matrix, or three-layer argument. Sample metadata must be handled in a separate validated preprocessing step if needed.",
      "By default lambda1 and lambda2 are estimated by estimate_penalty_parameters_dragon. Manual shrinkage is allowed only when both values are supplied in [0, 1].",
      "output_format=matrix writes a labeled symmetric partial-correlation matrix. output_format=edge_list writes one undirected row per pair with source, target, partial_correlation, and precision.",
      "DRAGON output is aggregate, not sample-specific. Its partial correlations and precision values represent conditional associations, not causal relationships.",
      "Direct handoffs to PANDA, PUMA, LIONESS, CONDOR, BONOBO, and OTTER are illegal because their verified input contracts differ. A future pairwise/chained workflow requires an explicit conversion artifact and user confirmation.",
      "Require at least three samples in each layer before execution."
    ],
